questions.questionText:
In a certain code language,

&lsquo;A + B&rsquo; means &lsquo;A is the son of B&rsquo;

&lsquo;A &ndash; B&rsquo; means &lsquo;A is the brother of B&rsquo;

&lsquo;A x B&rsquo; means &lsquo;A is the wife of B&rsquo;

&lsquo;A &divide; B&rsquo; means &lsquo;A is the father of B&rsquo;

Based on the above, how is M related to Q if &lsquo;M + N &ndash; O &divide; P × Q&rsquo;?

